{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1499471-the-lost-gods-of-england","id":1499471,"title":"The Lost Gods of England","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-12T14:22:27-08:00","id":1499471,"title":"The Lost Gods of England","content":"Brian Branston's book The Lost Gods of England is older, first published in 1957, but it's core thesis is useful. The key element is that Branston sees the Norse Mythos as we have it as a late development heavily influenced by the rise of the Vikings. <br /> <br /> His evidence is that the Anglo-Saxon pagans seem to have known nothing of Ragnarok. The Anglo-Saxons at no time suggest that Odin is king of the gods and never use the term Allfather for Odin. Similarly, it's not Odin but Tiwas/Tyr that gets swallowed by the Fenriswulf. And Tiwas/Tyr gets rescued. His evidence for these assertions is well stated, I'll leave it to you to see if you are convinced, but it sets up a campaign idea. <br /> <br /> If sagas of the Anglo-Saxon gods could be found, or at least enough Anglo-Saxon literature to show that Ragnarok was a late literary convention unrelated to Norse mythology, Odin's fate might be changed. The plan is to use time travel (difficult and dangerous even for gods) to gain a stash of books in the ancient world that would rewrite literary history to favor and end to several fate bindings.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha and the Theoi are willing to join the plan. The Tuatha want to get their creation myth back plus other things. The Theoi have several volumes of poetry they want back in circulation.<br /> <br /> The avatars of several different gods, from three different pantheons striving to shatter fate bindings through poetry and legend.<br /> <br /> They will be opposed.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on how to make this campaign idea work? <br /> <br /> Suggestions. Polite suggestions welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T14:38:22-08:00","id":1499472,"title":"","content":"Maybe not exactly what you are looking for, but I think you could do a pretty interesting all Aesir campaign where all of the PCs are Incarnations of their Saxon mantles deliberately trying to replay their stories but with the ending changed and their doom avoided, effectively recasting their entire pantheon so it no longer includes Ragnar\u00f6k. <br /> <br /> And as an aside, I really would enjoy seeing the Saxon version of the Aesir, similar to how the Loa were in Mysteries of the World. Perhaps as part of the Welsh/Arthurian book.<br /> <br /> But for a purely time travel campaign, maybe Atlantean-tech time machine? Or alternatively, having to make a deal with Cronus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T11:10:50-08:00","id":1499549,"title":"","content":"I would like to run this from the other end of the campaign - the Shen opposing attempts to alter time, seeing it as attempting to break cause and effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26003-richard-the-lyin-heart","name":"Richard the Lyin' Heart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T12:37:45-08:00","id":1499562,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an interesting idea. I could see Odin resisting the whole thing for two reasons. First, so much of his mythic history and identity is bound up with preparing for Ragnarok. Two, it would end with Tyr being leaders of the Aesir, not him. So the Aesir might need to do an end run around their chief god to keep from being wiped out.<br /> <br /> Even in the period we have good records of Norse mythology for, Tyr was the god who oversaw the Thing, the democratic assembly of free men. The Romans equated Wotan (Odin) not with Jupiter, Mars or some other chief god, but with Mercury. It seems pretty likely that among the Germanic peoples--including the Anglo-Saxons--Tiwaz (Tyr) was chief god, as leader of the tribal assembly, while Odin was associated, like Mercury, with death and magic. Odin's rise to chief god historically seems to have been tied to the rise of a hereditary aristocracy, who adopted Odin as god of death and battle as their patron. Interestingly, in late pagan Iceland--which had no hereditary aristocracy--Odin's importance in the pantheon was declining in favor of Thor, the patron god of free men.<br /> <br /> So, if the Aesir's Anglo-Saxon Mantles become predominant, they might be saved from Ragnarok but end up with a different leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T17:05:20-08:00","id":1499587,"title":"","content":"Odin sacrificing power and prestige would be a major drawback. But remember, we're talking about Odin. He'll have a scram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T08:46:24-08:00","id":1499653,"title":"","content":"Very true. I could see him going along with to ensure victory in Ragnarok and find a way to still stay the Allfather. Draft Loki to help him rewrite the texts their rescuing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T09:55:06-08:00","id":1499656,"title":"","content":"Odin is likely working to get the older saner Loki back. But as Odin is notoriously shrewd and pragmatic, I see him working to ditch Ragnarok first. Gain new respect and allies next. Getting to be King of the Gods can wait. Maybe an EU like cross pantheon alliance with Hecate, Athena, Brigid, Bast, and Mannanan Mac Lir as his key allies. Odin loves prestige, he lives for power. Wisdom and knowledge are his preferred tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}